# Testing

## Framework

- No GTest / Catch2. Tests are custom C++ executables registered with CTest.
- Register via `ADD_TEST_TARGET` / `ADD_TEST_EXEC` in `cmake/Utils.cmake`.
- Fail with non-zero exit / clear stderr messages (see `tests/libswcdb_core/`).

## Layout

- `tests/libswcdb_core/` — unit tests for `swcdb_core`
- `tests/libswcdb/` — unit tests for `libswcdb` (include `SWC_IMPL_SOURCE` variants when relevant)
- `tests/integration/` — needs installed prefix + `swcdb_cluster` (Fabric/SSH)
- Golden output: `tests/testutils/testdiff` vs `.golden` files

## Running

```bash
make test
# or: ctest --output-on-failure in the build tree
```

Integration prerequisites: `make install`, writable data dirs, passwordless SSH for `swcdb_cluster`. Prefer unit tests under `libswcdb*` for local changes; extend integration only when cluster behavior is involved.
